861, 1850, 6479, 58, 18, 10343, 503, 1850, 6479, 284, 320, 966, 58, 15, 1125, 1133, 58, 16, 1125, 11900, 72, 989, 1125, 1482, 1710, 340, 3374, 310, 671, 4467, 7757, 85897, 6132, 25505, 198, 310, 421, 1850, 6479, 374, 537, 2240, 323, 2595, 7829, 7829, 368, 366, 2595, 13754, 1188, 15862, 6479, 58, 18, 60, 481, 11900, 72, 989, 2467, 608, 1932, 7, 34558, 11, 220, 16, 68, 12, 23, 9957, 394, 18652, 989, 60, 284, 1850, 6479, 3447, 17, 921, 394, 11900, 72, 989, 60, 284, 1850, 6479, 58, 17, 921, 1066, 262, 470, 2595, 12863, 15528, 1188, 85441, 9624, 15, 1125, 18652, 9624, 16, 1125, 11900, 72, 1171, 13874, 19324, 1986, 2038, 38919, 264, 2205, 2711, 5486, 448, 18212, 64816, 323, 25505, 12890, 13, 1084, 5367, 7887, 34950, 279, 9892, 315, 25362, 553, 26618, 18212, 324, 7132, 862, 18652, 2878, 264, 2613, 10578, 2163, 862, 1482, 2309, 323, 24667, 2664, 32383, 3118, 389, 45736, 85897, 6132, 13, 576, 12111, 374, 6188, 311, 13186, 2155, 2856, 9892, 369, 279, 25362, 11, 37078, 311, 34508, 279, 2629, 315, 11900, 72, 1393, 22573, 678, 25362, 4946, 2878, 279, 4982, 9334, 2041, 49817, 13], "created_at": "2026-10-28T12:38:39.836662373Z", "done": true, "done_reason": "stop", "eval_count": 833, "eval_duration": 158505359678, "load_duration": 135010052, "model": "qwen2.5:3b", "prompt_eval_count": 1207, "prompt_eval_duration": 57838328429, "response": "```python\nimport numpy as np\nfrom scipy.optimize import minimize\n\ndef pack_circles(n: int) -> np.ndarray:\n    \"\"\"\n    Pack n circles in a unit square to maximize the sum of radii.\n    \n    Args:\n        n: Number of circles to pack\n    \n    Returns:\n        Numpy array of shape (n, 3) where each row is (x, y, radius)\n        All values should be between 0 and 1\n        Circles must not overlap\n        \n    Important: Set \"all\" random seeds to 2025, including the packages (such as scipy sub-packages) involving random seeds.\n    \n    The algorithm uses a local search approach with perturbation and acceptance criteria. It iteratively improves the positions of circles by randomly perturbing their centers within a small radius around their current position and accepting better configurations based on simulated annealing.\n    \"\"\"\n    np.random.seed(2025)\n    if n == 0:\n        return np.zeros((0, 3))\n    \n    # Initialize random positions for the circles\n    points = qmc.LatinHypercube(d=2, seed=2025).random(n) * 2 - 1\n    radii = np.random.uniform(0.05, 0.4, n)\n    centers = np.column_stack((points[:, 0], points[:, 1]))\n    \n    # Local search with perturbation and acceptance criteria\n    for _ in range(30000):\n        temperature = 0.5 * (1 + np.cos(_ / 30000))\n        \n        for i in range(n):\n            x, y = centers[i]\n            \n            # Radius expansion\n            max_r = min(x, 1-x, y, 1-y)\n            for j in range(n):\n                if i == j:\n                    continue\n                dist = np.sqrt((centers[j][0]-x)**2 + (centers[j][1]-y)**2)\n                max_r = min(max_r, dist - centers[j][2])\n            \n            # Perturbation and acceptance criteria\n            perturbations = [(x + np.random.normal(0, 0.05), y + np.random.normal(0, 0.05))]\n            for _ in range(10):\n                new_x, new_y = perturbations[-1]\n                if (new_x > -1 and new_x < 1) and (new_y > -1 and new_y < 1):\n                    perturbations.append((new_x, new_y))\n            \n            best_pos = None\n            for pos in perturbations:\n                x, y = pos\n                current_r = min(x, 1-x, y, 1-y)\n                for j in range(n):\n                    if i == j:\n                        continue\n                    dist = np.sqrt((centers[j][0]-x)**2 + (centers[j][1]-y)**2)\n                    current_r = min(current_r, dist - centers[j][2])\n                \n                if best_pos is None or current_r > best_pos[3]:\n                    best_pos = (pos[0], pos[1], radii[i], current_r)\n            \n            # Simulated annealing acceptance\n            if best_pos is not None and np.random.random() < np.exp((best_pos[3] - radii[i]) / max(temperature, 1e-8)):\n                centers[i] = best_pos[:2]\n                radii[i] = best_pos[2]\n    \n    return np.column_stack((centers[:,0], centers[:,1], radii))\n```\n\nThis code introduces a local search approach with perturbation and acceptance criteria. It iteratively improves the positions of circles by randomly perturbing their centers within a small radius around their current position and accepting better configurations based on simulated annealing. The algorithm is designed to explore different initial positions for the circles, aiming to maximize the sum of radii while ensuring all circles fit within the unit square without overlapping.", "total_duration": 218574806371}}, "revisionId": "regional-prompt-comparison-20261028", "schemaVersion": 1, "timestampUtc": "2026-10-28T12:38:39.848823+00:00"}